/bootstrap.ts`)\n  runs at the start of every `review` / bare `roast` with a toplevel\n  config. Without terminals it records `roast.gate-notice=sent`; with\n  `simulateTerminals(t, true)` it reads the first stdin line. A review\n  test that feeds stdin to a later prompt (trust, keys) must first record\n  `roast.gate` or set `gate.offer: false`, or account for the offer\n  taking that line. Offer tests are in `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HMXzVL3gP8Hj7fwaZPGuUt","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-30-gate-offer-during-review/docs/agents/gate.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bd047a4-2a9e-4212-bc74-c03950f158ae","uuid":"1fbe3105-d65a-4362-82e3-4bf5c61d6264","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:56:36.820Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-30-gate-offer-during-review/docs/agents/gate.md","oldString":"- `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.","newString":"- `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.\n- The review-time offer (`src/cli/gate-offer.ts`, `src/gate/bootstrap.ts`)\n  runs at the start of every `review` / bare `roast` with a toplevel\n  config. Without terminals it records `roast.gate-notice=sent`; with\n  `simulateTerminals(t, true)` it reads the first stdin line. A review\n  test that feeds stdin to a later prompt (trust, keys) must first record\n  `roast.gate` or set `gate.offer: false`, or account for the offer\n  taking that line. Offer tests are in `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`.","originalFile":"# Gate\n\nGo: `internal/gate`, `internal/cli/gate.go`. TS: `src/gate/`.\n\n## Hook behavior\n\n- The hook (`internal/gate/pre-commit.sh`, embedded as `HookScript`)\n  runs only `node_modules/.bin/roast` at the Git toplevel, never `PATH`.\n  It first calls the hidden `roast gate settings` (prints\n  `timeout_seconds=` and `severity=` lines from the config's `gate`\n  section, defaults 180/HIGH), then `roast review --staged ...\n  --max-severity <severity>`. Any failure, including a settings query\n  that exits non-zero, warns and allows the commit; only review exit 1\n  blocks.\n- The hook runs from the Git toplevel without `--config`, so it sees\n  only a toplevel `.roast.json` (`gateConfigPath` in\n  `internal/cli/config.go`). `gate enable` refuses and the review-time\n  bootstrap stays silent without one; `gate enable` tests write a\n  toplevel config first.\n- Installed hooks are refreshed by content comparison with the script,\n  so editing it needs no version bump.\n- TS `HOOK_SCRIPT` is `internal/gate/pre-commit.sh` through the text\n  loader (byte-identical, so Go-installed hooks are not stale).\n  `hook.ts` handles hook bodies as `Buffer`s so strip keeps every\n  foreign byte. Hook writes use `fsutil` `writeFileAtomic` with `mode`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Go hook execution tests (`hook_exec_test.go`) drive a real\n  `git commit` with a shell stub that `newStub(t, repo...)` writes at\n  each repo's `node_modules/.bin/roast`. It answers `gate settings` from\n  `STUB_TIMEOUT` / `STUB_SEVERITY` and logs only the review call\n  (`ARGS:` plus the staged diff), so `stub.ran` is empty when no review\n  happened.\n- TS gate tests build repos with `gateRepo(t)` (`test/gate/helpers.ts`:\n  global/system git config cut out, maintenance off, toplevel\n  `.roast.json`); hook execution tests use `seededRepo`, `newStub`, and\n  `commit` from `test/gate/exec-helpers.ts`.\n- Simulate a non-local `roast.gate` with\n  `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0`, never a global file.\n- `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":39,"oldLines":3,"newStart":39,"newLines":10,"lines":[" - Simulate a non-local `roast.gate` with","   `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`KEY_0`/`VALUE_0`, never a global file."," - `ROAST_TEST_SKIP_GATE_TIMEOUT=1` skips the sleeping tests.","+- The review-time offer (`src/cli/gate-offer.ts`, `src/gate/bootstrap.ts`)","+  runs at the start of every `review` / bare `roast` with a toplevel","+  config. Without terminals it records `roast.gate-notice=sent`; with","+  `simulateTerminals(t, true)` it reads the first stdin line. A review","+  test that feeds stdin to a later prompt (trust, keys) must first record","+  `roast.gate` or set `gate.offer: false`, or account for the offer","+  taking that line. Offer tests are in `test/cli/gate-offer.ts`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HMXzVL3gP8Hj7fwaZPGuUt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
