{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UkRA6hCtrwidvhQvetpLRK","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-30-gate-offer-during-review/.redeye/notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bd047a4-2a9e-4212-bc74-c03950f158ae","uuid":"b28e2a49-fb88-413f-a299-826aab22fca3","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:13:08.018Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/roast.ts-rewrite-30-gate-offer-during-review/.redeye/notes.md","oldString":"## Existing tests","newString":"## Final gate\n`npm test` passed (6700/6700), and lint and typecheck are clean. The first\n`npm run test:go` failed once in TestOpenRouterLoginClosesTheListenerOnEveryPath\n(exchange_failure: callback GET got EOF). This branch has no Go changes. The\ntest passed 8 runs in a row on its own, and the next full `test:go` passed\n(exit 0). It is a flaky localhost race and not related to this ticket.\n\n## Existing tests","originalFile":"# Ticket 30 notes (gate offer during review)\n\n## Seams\nSession was non-interactive, so the seams come from spec 12 section 5\n(\"Bootstrap\"): the CLI seam `runRoast(['review', ...])` via\n`settingsRepo` against the fake chat server, with `simulateTerminals`\nand stdin answers. Outcomes are read from local git config and hook\nfiles. One test uses the lower module seam (`bootstrap()` in\ntest/gate/bootstrap.ts) for \"hint printed once\": through the CLI the\nsecond run rewrites the same `roast.gate-notice=sent` value, so dropping\nthe `noticeSent` guard could not be seen in git config.\n\n## Implementation\n- src/gate/bootstrap.ts: a direct port of internal/gate/bootstrap.go\n  (`bootstrap`, `Outcome`, `BootstrapOptions`). `out` takes one line;\n  the CLI adds the `roast: ` prefix.\n- src/gate/hook.ts: `refreshOwnedSidecar` is now exported.\n- src/cli/gate-offer.ts: `maybeBootstrapGate(ctx)`. It skips on\n  `--error-format json` (run.ts validates `--error-format` before\n  calling the handler, so the order in spec 01 3.4 holds), finds only\n  `<toplevel>/.roast.json` through `gateConfigPath`, and does a raw\n  `loadConfig` (no trust check, no stored credentials). Every failure is\n  silent, or printed as `pre-commit gate setup skipped` when bootstrap\n  throws. An abort is rethrown.\n- src/cli/review.ts: the no-op stub is removed. The handler shared by\n  `review` and `$0` calls the real `maybeBootstrapGate` first.\n- The ticket names `src/cli/gate-offer.ts` and spec 12 names\n  `bootstrap-gate.ts`. I followed the ticket.\n\n## Readings\n- \"A second review with terminals simulated does not consume any stdin\n  for the offer\": checked with a counting Readable (reads == 0). Trust is\n  already approved, so nothing else reads stdin.\n- `GIT_INDEX_FILE` test: set to the repo's real `.git/index`, so the\n  review's own git calls still work.\n- \"Inherited shared gate\": core.hooksPath points at a temp dir that\n  holds a legacy Roast dispatcher. Non-interactive leaves roast.gate\n  unset. Interactive with EOF records `declined`, never `enabled`.\n- Bootstrap failure: `.git/hooks` is chmod 0555 and the answer is `y`.\n  The review exits 0 and still reaches the fake server.\n\n## Mutation checks\nEach mutation below failed at least one test: dropping noOffer, the\nGIT_INDEX_FILE guard, the declined->quiet return, recordNotice, the\nerrorFormat json skip, the toplevel-only lookup, the real config load,\nthe prompt presence, the sidecar refresh, the stale-dispatcher install,\nand the noticeSent guard (module test).\n\nOne mutation survived: dropping `decision !== 'enabled'` from step 4.\nFor an enabled repo, step 6 refreshes the same way, so the change has no\nvisible effect.\n\n## Existing tests\ntest/cli/review-trust.ts \"inline trust prompt\" still passes. Its first\nrun answers with EOF, which declines the gate offer and records\n`declined`, so every later answer goes to the trust prompt.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":50,"oldLines":6,"newStart":50,"newLines":13,"lines":[" For an enabled repo, step 6 refreshes the same way, so the change has no"," visible effect."," ","+## Final gate","+`npm test` passed (6700/6700), and lint and typecheck are clean. The first","+`npm run test:go` failed once in TestOpenRouterLoginClosesTheListenerOnEveryPath","+(exchange_failure: callback GET got EOF). This branch has no Go changes. The","+test passed 8 runs in a row on its own, and the next full `test:go` passed","+(exit 0). It is a flaky localhost race and not related to this ticket.","+"," ## Existing tests"," test/cli/review-trust.ts \"inline trust prompt\" still passes. Its first"," run answers with EOF, which declines the gate offer and records"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UkRA6hCtrwidvhQvetpLRK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLwiRoKRY4XfTTstU21f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] With terminals simulated and stdin `y\\n`, a review in a repo with a toplevel approved config installs the hook and sets `roast.gate=enabled`. The review then proceeds against the fake server.\n[x] With stdin `n\\n`, `roast.gate=declined` is recorded and no hook is written. A second review with terminals simulated does not consume any stdin for the offer.\n[x] Without terminals, the first review sets `roast.gate-notice=sent` and writes no hook. A second review leaves the config unchanged.\n[x] `GIT_INDEX_FILE` set in `io.env` suppresses the offer: no `roast.gate*` keys change.\n[x] `gate.offer: false` neither prompts nor hints and leaves `roast.gate-notice` unset.\n[x] `ROAST_NO_HOOK=1` in `io.env` does not stop the offer.\n[x] A config only in a subdirectory gives no offer. A toplevel config gives one, also under `--format json`. `--error-format json` gives none.\n[x] A toplevel config that fails to load gives no offer, and the review exits 2 with the config error.\n[x] A declined repo with a stale legacy shared dispatcher gets the dispatcher refreshed. An inherited shared gate in a repo with no local decision is not adopted (`roast.gate` stays unset).\n[x] A bootstrap failure, such as an unwritable hooks directory after a yes, does not change the review's exit code.\n[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\nTicket 30 is done: `roast review` and bare `roast` now offer the pre-commit gate before the review starts. All tests pass. The first Go test run failed once in an unrelated test, which I cover below.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `src/gate/bootstrap.ts` ports the Go `Bootstrap` directly, covering `bootstrap`, `Outcome` and `BootstrapOptions`.\n- `src/cli/gate-offer.ts` adds `maybeBootstrapGate`. It does nothing under `--error-format json`. It looks only at `<toplevel>/.roast.json`, loads it without a trust check, and asks only when terminals are detected, reading the answer from the shared line reader. If the gate setup throws, Roast prints a `pre-commit gate setup skipped` warning and the review goes on. A Ctrl-C abort is still passed through.\n- `src/cli/review.ts` calls it at the top of the handler that serves both `review` and bare `roast`. This replaces the earlier no-op stub. The `--error-format` value is already validated before the handler runs, so the ordering the spec asks for holds.\n- `refreshOwnedSidecar` in `src/gate/hook.ts` is now exported so the bootstrap can use it.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `test/cli/gate-offer.ts` checks each item above through the in-process CLI against the fake server. It reads results from local git config and hook files, plus a counter on stdin reads to prove the offer asks nothing. One more test checks that bare `roast` gets the offer.\n- `test/gate/bootstrap.ts` checks that the non-interactive hint prints only once. Through the CLI this was invisible: the second run rewrites the same `roast.gate-notice=sent`, so a guard I deliberately broke went unnoticed.\n- The bootstrap went in as one direct port, so later tests passed immediately rather than failing first. To show they still check something, I broke each guard in turn. Every break failed a test except one: dropping `decision !== 'enabled'` from step 4. That change has no visible effect, because an enabled repo is refreshed by the install step anyway.\n\n**Results:** `npm test` passed 6700/6700, and lint and typecheck are clean. The first full `npm run test:go` failed once in `TestOpenRouterLoginClosesTheListenerOnEveryPath`: a callback request got `EOF`. This branch changes no Go code. The test then passed 8 runs in a row on its own, and the next full `test:go` passed with exit 0, so it looks like a flaky race in that test.\n\n**Note for review tests:** any review test that simulates terminals now gets the gate prompt first, and it reads the first stdin line. The existing inline trust-prompt test still passes only because its first answer is end-of-input, which declines the offer. I added this to `docs/agents/gate.md`.\n\nThere are three commits on the branch. `.redeye/notes.md` is left uncommitted, as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":135594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":374},"output_tokens":780,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bd047a4-2a9e-4212-bc74-c03950f158ae","uuid":"8b624ced-946a-4fd0-b098-b7a01085dddf","timestamp":"2026-11-24T02:13:20.654Z","request_id":"req_011ChLwiRetb8vqoK9cmoRX6"}
